Hence it is apparent that the rule never makes an error exceeding ·3 vib., and generally keeps below this limit. Now at 256 an error of ·3 vib. amounts to 2 cents, and at 540 to less than 1 cent. The rule, therefore, properly handled will give results equal if not @@R@@
